  "body": "Check the work height against each stated wire guide before the post writes NC. Compare both heights in world coordinates. Use the operation, the part and the stock to determine the full work height.\n\nA 3 degree taper through 12 mm of stock previously posted 496 bytes with its upper guide at Z5. The normal CLI now refuses this case and creates no output file. A 0.001 mm overrun also fails. A fractional setup origin that puts the work exactly at the guide passes.\n\nThe valid vertical and tapered control programs match their original NC files byte for byte. A straight cut still accepts a machine with no stated guide heights.\n\nThe pinning tests are work_above_the_upper_guide_blocks_the_post and the shifted-stock test in wire_taper. The quick gate passed all six steps, including all 291 app library tests. The verification also used the normal command script, all 10 related wire suites (62 tests), and strict clippy on all camcraft-app targets.\n\nThe offline 40 by 20 mm punch comparison used the same nominal geometry in three tools. The two Agie generators agreed on the nominal contour. CamCraft put its wire center 0.165 mm outside each face. The offline Agie control formally checked and plotted its native vertical bundle. Its technology added its own trim offsets. It did not run the CamCraft generic program or verify a tapered cut.\n\nThe current head is 06925e8c4. It includes the upstream Apple silicon release fixture from #2934 through a clean merge. The full quick gate passed 6/6 steps in 15.1 minutes on that head. The optimized pocket3d_hsm bore test now passes with 3158 moves, 3130 planar moves and 1141 arcs. The complete reached heavy gate is running.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: Wire EDM refuses a post when the work extends past a stated guide height.\n\nFixes #2923\n\n",
